<%# Signed-in preview banner (spec §6.4): PreviewController is the only place
    that sets @preview_record, so this only ever renders there, via
    pages/show.html.erb's `content_for :preview_banner`. A page's "Edit" goes
    to CS Studio's own page editor (Task 4); a post's now goes to CS
    Studio's own post editor too (Task 7), replacing the Avo link this
    banner used until then. "View live" only appears once the record is
    actually live; linking to its public address while it's still a draft
    or scheduled would be a dead end. %>
<div role="status" class="mt-4 rounded-cs border border-warn bg-warn-tint px-3 py-2 font-cs-mono text-label uppercase tracking-mono text-warn-ink">
  <span>Preview · <%= @preview_record.status.humanize %> — not visible to visitors</span>
  <%= link_to "Edit", (@post ? admin_post_path(@post) : admin_page_path(@page)), class: "ml-2 underline" %>
  <% if @preview_record.live? %>
    <%= link_to "View live", PublicSite::Urls.new.path_for(@preview_record), class: "ml-2 underline" %>
  <% end %>
</div>
